{number: 122}
{title: A Wonderful Savior}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
A [C] wonderful Savior is Jesus my Lord,
A [F] wonderful Savior to [C] me;
He hideth my soul in the cleft of the rock,
Where [G7] rivers of pleasure I [C] see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
He [C] hideth my soul in the cleft of the rock
That [F] shadows a dry, thirsty [C] land;
He hideth my life in the depths of His love,
And [G7] covers me there with His [C] hand,
And [F] covers me [C] there with His [G7] [C] hand.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
A [C] wonderful Savior is Jesus my Lord,
He [F] taketh my burden a-[C] way;
He holdeth me up, and I shall not be moved,
He [G7] giveth me strength as my [C] day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
With [C] numberless blessings each moment He crowns,
And, [F] filled with His fullness di-[C] vine,
I sing in my rapture, oh, glory to God
For [G7] such a Redeemer as [C] mine!
{end_of_verse}
